<DocLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Dazzlit"
  description="How Dazzlit collects, uses and protects your information when you use dazzlit.com."
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  updated="16 November 2026"
>
  <p>
    Dazzlit is a global digital marketing agency. This policy explains what
    information we collect through dazzlit.com, how we use it, and the choices
    you have. If you have questions about this policy, contact us through the
    form on our contact page.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <p>When you ask us for a free proposal, we collect the details you give us: your name, work email, website, the services you are interested in, your main market and your monthly marketing budget. We also collect the page you submitted the form from.</p>
  <p>When you browse the site, we collect anonymous usage information through analytics, as described below. We do not collect payment details through this website.</p>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <p>We use proposal requests to prepare your proposal and to reply to you. We use anonymous analytics to understand which pages are useful and to improve the site. We do not sell your personal information, and we do not share it with other companies for their marketing.</p>

  <h2>Where it is stored</h2>
  <p>Proposal requests are stored in Cloudflare D1, the database for this site, and are emailed to us through Resend so we can respond. Our site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages, and spam protection on the form is provided by Cloudflare Turnstile. We have not connected a customer relationship management system yet; when we do, proposal requests will also be stored there, and this policy will be updated.</p>

  <h2>Analytics and cookies</h2>
  <p>We use Google Analytics 4 only if you accept cookies, and Cloudflare Web Analytics, which does not use cookies. You can change your cookie choice at any time from our cookies page. See our <a href="/cookies/">cookies page</a> for the full list.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>We keep proposal requests only as long as we need them to respond to you and to keep a record of the enquiry. You can ask us to delete your details at any time by contacting us through the form on our contact page.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to ask for a copy of your information, to correct it, to delete it, or to object to how we use it. We will respond to such requests within a reasonable time.</p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy when the site or our practices change, for example when we connect a customer relationship management system or add new tools. The date at the top of this page shows when it was last updated.</p>
</DocLayout>
